"""Build a readable report from solved numerical outputs, without changing them."""
from pathlib import Path
import html
import json

HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent


def build_report():
    result = json.loads((HERE / "results/summary.json").read_text())
    verification = json.loads((HERE / "results/solver_verification.json").read_text())
    levels, geometry, config = result["levels"], result["geometry"], result["configuration"]
    last = levels[-1]
    format_change = lambda value: "—" if value is None else f"{value:.3f}%"
    headers = ["Target h (mm)", "Tetrahedra", "Geometric vertices", "P2 field nodes", "DOFs",
               "Centre abs(uz) (mm)", "Probe mean VM (MPa)", "Deflection change", "Probe stress change"]
    rows = [[f"{r['target_mesh_size_mm']:g}", f"{r['tetrahedra']:,}", f"{r['geometric_vertices']:,}",
             f"{r['p2_nodes']:,}", f"{r['displacement_dofs']:,}", f"{abs(r['center_uz_mm']):.7f}",
             f"{r['central_patch_mean_vm_mpa']:.6f}", format_change(r['deflection_change_percent']),
             format_change(r['probe_stress_change_percent'])] for r in levels]
    criterion = "met" if result["successive_mesh_criterion_met"] else "not met"
    markdown_table = "| " + " | ".join(headers) + " |\n| " + " | ".join(["---"] * len(headers)) + " |\n"
    markdown_table += "\n".join("| " + " | ".join(row) + " |" for row in rows)
    body = f"""# Preliminary enclosure-lid FEA

The study contains actual finite-element solves of the lid extracted from the supplied STEP assembly. The material and loading were undecided, so the user authorized a preliminary assumed study. These results are conditional on the setup below; no material-strength or product-safety pass is claimed.

[Visual report](Report.html) · [Configuration](study.json) · [Complete mesh statistics](results/mesh_statistics.csv) · [Machine-readable results](results/summary.json)

## Geometry and assumptions

| Item | Study definition |
| --- | --- |
| Geometry | Actual named lid from [VKA2026.step](../../cad/VKA2026.step), 100 × 70 × 3 mm, four 3.5 mm diameter holes. |
| Source pose | Exploded lid translated by -37 mm in z to the analysis position z=0..3 mm; shape unchanged. |
| Material | Assumed homogeneous isotropic linear-elastic polymer, E={config['youngs_modulus_mpa']:g} MPa and Poisson ratio {config['poisson_ratio']:g}. No material grade or print-process properties selected. |
| Load | {config['total_downward_force_n']:g} N uniformly downward over the meshed top face; final pressure {last['pressure_mpa']:.8f} MPa. This is an illustrative loading scenario. |
| Supports | All three displacement components fixed on the four cylindrical screw-hole walls. These idealized rigid supports omit fastener/contact flexibility. |
| Formulation | 3-D small-displacement linear elasticity; quadratic displacement tetrahedra over straight-sided tetrahedral geometry. Units: mm, N, MPa. |
| Excluded | Enclosure base, electronics, helmet, bolts/preload, gasket contact, impact/drop, fatigue, creep, plasticity, thermal and sealing qualification. |

The imported enclosure is 100 × 70 × 25 mm. It differs from the submission's 52 × 88 × 28 mm target; this study uses the actual supplied lid and does not resolve that packaging difference.

![Geometry, load and supports](results/plots/setup.png)

## Mesh statistics and convergence

{markdown_table}

The configured preliminary criterion is less than {config['comparison_tolerance_percent']:g}% change in both selected response measures for {config['required_successive_comparisons']} successive refinements, with at least {config['minimum_mesh_levels']} mesh levels. That criterion was **{criterion}**. Percentage change is `100 * abs(new - previous) / abs(new)`.

Deflection is evaluated at the fixed physical centre (50, 35, 1.5) mm. The stress measure is the arithmetic mean of von Mises stress at nine fixed physical points with x=48/50/52 mm, y=33/35/37 mm, and z=2.7 mm. It is **not the maximum stress in the lid**. The field is evaluated directly without nodal stress smoothing.

Geometric vertices are the nodes stored in the first-order Gmsh mesh. P2 field nodes include the edge displacement nodes generated by scikit-fem; each has three displacement DOFs. Curved hole walls are approximated by planar facets. The target h is an upper mesh-size control, not the size of every element; curved features receive local refinement. This successive-mesh check does not bound every geometric or solution error.

![Actual convergence plots](results/plots/convergence.png)

![Final surface mesh](results/plots/mesh_{last['level']}.png)

## Results under the assumed setup

- Centre downward displacement: **{abs(last['center_uz_mm']):.7f} mm**.
- Fixed central-patch mean von Mises stress: **{last['central_patch_mean_vm_mpa']:.6f} MPa**.
- Largest sampled quadrature-point von Mises stress: {last['global_quadrature_max_vm_mpa']:.6f} MPa. Peaks near idealized clamps can be mesh-sensitive; this value is not used as a converged strength result.
- Applied z force: {last['applied_force_z_n']:.9f} N; support z reaction: {last['support_reaction_z_n']:.9f} N.
- Final mesh minimum SICN: {last['quality_min_SICN']:.4f}; fifth percentile: {last['quality_p05_SICN']:.4f}. Higher positive SICN indicates better conditioning under this metric; it is not a universal acceptance threshold.

No yield/ultimate strength was selected, so no factor of safety or strength pass/fail was calculated. The centre displacement is about {100 * abs(last['center_uz_mm']) / 3:.2f}% of the lid thickness in this scenario.

![Solved displacement and stress fields](results/plots/response.png)

## Numerical verification

Before solving the lid, the same elasticity assembly, traction loading, boundary-DOF treatment, and point-stress evaluation passed an independent unit-cube uniaxial-tension test against its analytical displacement and stress field. Relative displacement error: {verification['relative_displacement_error']:.3e}; maximum stress-component error: {verification['maximum_stress_component_error_mpa']:.3e} MPa. See [verification JSON](results/solver_verification.json).

Each lid solution was checked for global force balance and free-DOF residual. Final relative force-balance error: {last['force_balance_relative_error']:.3e}; relative free-DOF residual: {last['free_dof_relative_residual']:.3e}. These are numerical checks, not experimental validation of the material, supports or loading.

## Open and reproduce

1. Open `Report.html` for the illustrated report.
2. Open `results/meshes/{last['level']}.msh` in Gmsh to inspect the tagged 3-D mesh. `loaded_top` and `screw_walls` identify the load and support surfaces.
3. Open `results/{last['level']}.vtu` in a VTK-compatible viewer to inspect vertex-sampled displacement and cell-average stress. This visualization uses the linear geometric mesh; full quadratic displacement coefficients are retained in the corresponding `_solution.npz` file.
4. To rerun from the repository root, use Python 3.12 in an isolated environment:

```bash
python -m venv .venv-fea
# Windows: .venv-fea\\Scripts\\python.exe
# macOS/Linux: .venv-fea/bin/python
.venv-fea\\Scripts\\python.exe -m pip install -r simulation/lid-pressure/requirements.txt
.venv-fea\\Scripts\\python.exe simulation/lid-pressure/run_study.py
```

The script selects the actual lid by its imported name, checks that it has four cylindrical holes, records source SHA-256, generates and solves meshes, checks forces, exports raw outputs, and rebuilds this report. Change `study.json` when the actual material and loading are selected. Absolute constants in this checked-in report describe the published study snapshot; review geometry/probe locations when changing the source geometry.

`run_study.py --verify-only` repeats the analytical solver/probe test. `run_study.py --plots-only` rebuilds figures and reports from the existing solved data. Re-running the full study overwrites its result files; `summary.json` identifies the mesh levels in the current run.

## Evidence and limits

The folder includes native STEP extraction, tagged Gmsh meshes, solver code/configuration, full displacement coefficients, VTU field exports, mesher logs, CSV statistics, JSON results, and PNG/SVG plots. These figures come from actual numerical solves; they are not screenshots of Fusion or evidence of physical fabrication.

The generic material has no assigned strength, anisotropy, print orientation, temperature dependence or manufacturing defects. The rigid hole-wall constraints can overestimate mounting stiffness. Experimental material data, actual service loads, realistic contacts, a suitable failure criterion, and physical validation are needed before a product-design decision. This study establishes no drop resistance, IP rating, helmet compliance or intrinsic-safety certification.

## Software and method references

- [Gmsh manual](https://gmsh.info/doc/texinfo/gmsh.html): STEP/OpenCASCADE import, tagged meshing and SICN mesh-quality metric.
- [scikit-fem 3-D elasticity example](https://github.com/kinnala/scikit-fem/blob/12.0.2/docs/examples/ex11.py): linear-elasticity formulation.
- [scikit-fem how-to](https://scikit-fem.readthedocs.io/en/stable/howto.html): boundary DOFs, postprocessing and field export.
- [Autodesk mesh convergence guidance](https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/ENU/Fusion-Simulate/files/SIM-MESH-CONVERGENCE.htm): compare consistent physical locations during refinement.

Software versions are recorded in `results/summary.json`; direct dependencies are pinned in `requirements.txt`. Source STEP SHA-256: `{geometry['source_step_sha256']}`.
"""
    (HERE / "README.md").write_text(body, encoding="utf-8")
    table = "<thead><tr>" + "".join(f"<th>{html.escape(x)}</th>" for x in headers) + "</tr></thead><tbody>"
    table += "".join("<tr>" + "".join(f"<td>{html.escape(x)}</td>" for x in row) + "</tr>" for row in rows) + "</tbody>"
    limitations = "".join(f"<li>{html.escape(x)}</li>" for x in config["limitations"])
    document = f"""<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>PRAN RAKSHAK | Preliminary lid FEA</title><style>
body{{margin:0;background:#edf2f4;color:#173042;font:16px/1.6 system-ui,Arial,sans-serif}}main{{max-width:1100px;margin:32px auto;background:white;padding:44px;border-radius:12px}}h1{{font-size:38px;line-height:1.2;margin:12px 0}}h2{{margin-top:40px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce6eb;padding-bottom:8px}}.tag{{color:#087f8c;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1px;font-size:12px}}.notice{{background:#fff5df;border-left:5px solid #d68619;padding:18px}}img{{width:100%;height:auto}}.scroll{{overflow-x:auto}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}}th,td{{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce6eb;text-align:right;white-space:nowrap}}th{{background:#edf5f5}}.metrics{{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;margin:24px 0}}.metric{{flex:1;min-width:220px;background:#edf5f5;padding:20px;border-radius:8px}}.metric strong{{display:block;font-size:28px;color:#087f8c}}a{{color:#087f8c}}code{{background:#edf2f4;padding:2px 4px}}@media print{{body{{background:white}}main{{padding:0;margin:0}}h2{{break-after:avoid}}img,table{{break-inside:avoid}}}}
</style></head><body><main><div class="tag">PRAN RAKSHAK / MECHANICAL STUDY</div><h1>Enclosure lid: mesh refinement and response</h1>
<p class="notice"><strong>Preliminary, assumption-based analysis.</strong> Actual STEP geometry and numerical solves; material, loading and rigid supports are illustrative. No material-strength or safety pass is claimed.</p>
<div class="metrics"><div class="metric">Centre deflection<strong>{abs(last['center_uz_mm']):.5f} mm</strong>Under {config['total_downward_force_n']:g} N assumed distributed load</div><div class="metric">Final tetrahedra<strong>{last['tetrahedra']:,}</strong>{last['displacement_dofs']:,} displacement DOFs</div><div class="metric">Selected mesh criterion<strong>{criterion.capitalize()}</strong>Two successive comparisons below {config['comparison_tolerance_percent']:g}%</div></div>
<h2>1. Geometry and study setup</h2><p>Named lid extracted from VKA2026.step: 100 × 70 × 3 mm, four 3.5 mm holes. Isotropic material E={config['youngs_modulus_mpa']:g} MPa, ν={config['poisson_ratio']:g}, both assumed. All displacement components fixed on the four screw-hole walls. Uniform downward top-face traction totals {config['total_downward_force_n']:g} N.</p><img src="results/plots/setup.png" alt="Actual geometry, supports and loading">
<h2>2. Mesh statistics</h2><div class="scroll"><table>{table}</table></div><p>Gmsh stores linear geometric vertices; the solver adds quadratic displacement edge nodes. h is the upper mesh-size control. Curved walls are faceted. Full statistics: <a href="results/mesh_statistics.csv">CSV</a>.</p>
<h2>3. Selected response convergence</h2><p>Centre displacement and mean von Mises stress at nine fixed central points, z=2.7 mm. These measures changed by {last['deflection_change_percent']:.3f}% and {last['probe_stress_change_percent']:.3f}% in the final comparison. This is a successive-mesh criterion, not an absolute error bound.</p><img src="results/plots/convergence.png" alt="Solved displacement and fixed-location stress across four meshes">
<h2>4. Final mesh</h2><img src="results/plots/mesh_{last['level']}.png" alt="Final top-surface mesh and counts">
<h2>5. Displacement and stress fields</h2><img src="results/plots/response.png" alt="Actual displacement and stress contours"><p>Central probe mean: {last['central_patch_mean_vm_mpa']:.6f} MPa. Largest quadrature-point sample: {last['global_quadrature_max_vm_mpa']:.6f} MPa, with clamp-region peaks that have not been established as converged strength values. No factor of safety is calculated.</p>
<h2>6. Numerical checks</h2><p>The analytical uniaxial-tension patch test passed: relative displacement error {verification['relative_displacement_error']:.3e}; stress-component error {verification['maximum_stress_component_error_mpa']:.3e} MPa. Final lid force-balance error {last['force_balance_relative_error']:.3e}; free-DOF residual {last['free_dof_relative_residual']:.3e}. These checks verify numerical behavior under the chosen model.</p>
<h2>7. Limits and next steps</h2><ul>{limitations}</ul><p>The actual enclosure is 100 × 70 × 25 mm; the submission's smaller pod envelope remains a target. Select the real material, manufacturing process and service loads, model actual fastener/contact behavior, and validate with physical tests before making a product decision.</p>
<h2>8. Reproducible files</h2><p><a href="README.md">Detailed report and rerun instructions</a> · <a href="study.json">Editable assumptions</a> · <a href="results/summary.json">Full results</a> · <a href="results/solver_verification.json">Analytical check</a> · <a href="results/meshes/{last['level']}.msh">Final tagged mesh</a> · <a href="results/{last['level']}.vtu">Field export</a></p><p>Source STEP SHA-256: <code style="overflow-wrap:anywhere">{geometry['source_step_sha256']}</code></p></main></body></html>"""
    (HERE / "Report.html").write_text(document, encoding="utf-8")
    print("Report.html and README.md generated from solved results.", flush=True)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    build_report()
